<!--
    Kuna: option itaniumeh on ARM32 (EHABI) and with types named from a
    type_info name string. P1 program prep reads .ARM.exidx: every entry is a
    function start (Thumb when decided), and a generic-model .ARM.extab entry
    holds the LSDA, whose type-table entries are R_ARM_TARGET2 words
    (`unlace-analysis/src/analyzers/entry/kuna_armexidx.rs`,
    `kuna_itaniumeh.rs`). The class Odd has hidden visibility, so only its
    type_info name string names it.

    Fixtures: `crates/unlace-analysis/tests/fixtures/ehcatch_x86_64.so`,
    `ehcatch_arm.so` and `ehcatch_thumb_stripped.so`, three builds of
    `ehcatch.cc` (clang 22 -O2 -fPIC -fexceptions, ld.lld -shared; the recipe
    is in the source):

      int guarded(int v) { try { work(v); } catch (int e) { return e; } return 0; }
      int sorted(int v) {
        try { work(v); }
        catch (const Odd &e) { return e.code; }
        catch (...) { return -1; }
        return twice(v);
      }

    `twice` is static, so the stripped Thumb build names it only through
    .ARM.exidx (0x103f6).
-->
